PART 3.  DEAN'S QUESTION, EXACTLY: AT 9, IS THE NEXT ANGLE UP, DOWN, OR BOTH?
==============================================================================
   R = rotation by H = pi/9. Nine steps:
     || R^9  + I ||                = 6.43e-16   -> R^9 = -I EXACTLY
     || R^18 - I ||                = 1.16e-15   -> R^18 = +I
     the LINE (projector vv^T) at step 9: ||P9 - P0|| = 8.95e-16  -> HOME
     the VECTOR at step 9:               ||R^9 v - v|| = 2.0000  -> ANTIPODAL

   So at step 9 the base is home and the fiber owes a sign. The shadow-closure
   EMITS EXACTLY ONE BIT. That bit is not bookkeeping -- it is the only record
   that the loop happened at all, and it lives nowhere in the circle. It lives
   on the axis. THAT is why the object is a helix.

   Now the three continuations Dean names:

     UP   (+pi/9, keep winding):  legal. the flow never stops. C1 satisfied.
     DOWN (-pi/9, reverse):       to reverse, the angular rate must go from
                                  + to -, and by Part 1 EVERY continuous path
                                  doing that touches omega = 0 -- the wall, the
                                  fixed point, the one thing C1 forbids.
                                  ==> DOWN IS ILLEGAL. NOT DISFAVOURED. ILLEGAL.
     BOTH:                        a single trajectory has ONE tangent; it cannot
                                  do both. Only an AMPLITUDE can carry both --
                                  and an amplitude carrying both branches of a
                                  Z2 label is precisely a superposition. The
                                  linkage (Part II) collapses it to one, and the
                                  which-way bit it reads IS the fiber sign above.

   ANSWER: UP. ALWAYS UP. And *which* up was never a choice -- it is a SELECTOR,
   fixed before the first step and unchangeable by any legal motion thereafter.
   The system cannot turn around. Not "does not." CANNOT.

