PART 4.  THE CONSEQUENCE C1 FORCES: HOMOCHIRALITY.
==============================================================================
   If handedness is a Z2 selector, then:
     - PERSISTENCE is FORCED: no legal motion crosses the wall, ever. Once a
       chirality is set, it is set for the lifetime of the flow. (Executed in
       Part 1: 2000/2000 crossing paths hit the forbidden set.)
     - SELECTION is OPEN: both rooms are legal. C1 says nothing about which.

   Every alpha-helix in every protein in every organism on Earth is RIGHT-handed.
   That is one of biology's oldest puzzles (homochirality; credited as open).
   C1's reading is not 'right-handed is better'. It is:

       handedness is an ORBIT LABEL, the biosphere is on ONE ORBIT, and no
       legal chemistry can cross the wall between them.

   The universality needs no advantage. It needs no selection pressure. It needs
   only that the wall is uncrossable -- which is C1, and which is executed above.
   PERSISTENCE: forced (CONFIRMED). WHICH ORBIT: open (Omega).
   [Dean's own protein work found alpha-helix periodicity at integer multiples
    of pi/9. The helix, the 9, and the handedness are the same object.]

